# Shared-node affinity monitor contract

**Activation:** `alwaysApply: false` — Read before editing matched paths.

## Compile flag

- `--enable-shared-node-multi-jid` (default **off**) defines `MONITOR_SHARED_NODE_MULTI_JID`.
- Shared build: no `stats_jobid` file read / `ev_stat` watcher.
- Default file build: unchanged; **never** emit `%jobs` / `%affinity`; **no** `host_mem_job` type.
- **Fleet RPM:** Horizon is the first shared-node cluster — `scripts/prepare_rpmbuild_horizon.sh` (`HPCS_BUNDLE_FLEET=horizon` / `scripts/fleet/horizon.force`) passes the flag via `build_static_bundle.sh`. Deploy listend before Horizon shared-node monitor RPMs.

## Discovery

- Group pids by cgroup v2 `slurmstepd.scope/<token>/`. Name sources, in order:
  1. `SLURM_JOB_ID` in a non-root pid's environ (env always wins).
  2. For a token still unnamed: the root `slurmstepd` title of the extern step — first pid of `<cgroup_root>/system.slice/slurmstepd.scope/<token>/step_extern/slurm/cgroup.procs`, then `/proc/<pid>/cmdline` = `slurmstepd: [<jid>.<step>]` or `[<jid>:namespace]` (`job_proc_jid_from_stepd_title`; all-digit jid). Sets `named_from_title`. Needed because the `/proc` walk skips root-owned pid dirs (`proc_filter`), so an idle allocation (only root stepds left) is otherwise never seen. Cost: one scandir of `slurmstepd.scope` plus two small reads per unnamed token per sample; fail-open on any miss.
- Every token (named or not) records that extern-step root stepd pid as `stepd_pid` (0 when `cgroup.procs` is missing or empty). Same file read as title naming; no extra cost for unnamed tokens, one small read per env-named token per sample.
- **CPU allocation (M1, 2026-11-03):** `job_emit_entry_cpulist` reads `sched_getaffinity(stepd_pid)` — the stepd sits in the job cgroup unpinned, so its mask is the job cpuset — and falls back to the union over ≤`affinity_pid_sample_limit` task pids only when `stepd_pid` is unknown or unreadable. Task pids alone under-report: MPI binds each rank to one core (hpcperfstats04, 2026-11-03: 9,589 of 15,475 `debug`-queue affinity rows were below the allocation, min 1 CPU). Still no `cpuset.cpus` reads.
- `jid_require_step_id` drops env-named groups without `SLURM_STEP_ID`; title-named groups are allocation presence and are kept.
- Token is never emitted. No cgroup `job_<id>` parse (Horizon tokens are opaque, e.g. `s4TDM6EWYAH400`).
- Store cgroup relpath (after `0::`) on each jid entry for memory reads; title-named entries use `/system.slice/slurmstepd.scope/<token>/step_extern/slurm`; empty on environ-only fallback.
- Never exec `scontrol` or `nvidia-smi`. Never `sched_setaffinity`.
- Never read `CUDA_VISIBLE_DEVICES`, `ROCR_VISIBLE_DEVICES`, or `ZE_AFFINITY_MASK`.
- Never walk `cpuset.cpus` / `cpuset.mems`.

## Wire

```text
%jobs jids=<csv>
%affinity jid=<jid> cpus=<list> gpus=<csv-or-> cg=<short>
host_mem_job j:<jid> [@fast|@full] <mem_used> <mem_peak> <anon_pages> <file_pages> <mapped> <dirty> <writeback> <page_tables>
```

- One sample block = one header jobid token (≤32 bare jid).
- **Sole jid holding every online CPU** (M2, 2026-11-03): ordinary unmarked payload with **every available GPU**, whatever its GPU grant (**still** may include `host_mem_job j:<jid>`). Slurm cannot start a second job on a node with no free CPU, so the node is the job's. The old rule also required `SLURM_JOB_GPUS` to equal the inventory, which marked whole-node jobs that requested no GPUs (`gpus=-`) and dropped every GPU row (jid 79282, 11 of 12 nodes). Unknown GPU inventory still takes the marked path.
- **Sole jid on part of the node** (M3, 2026-11-03): marked, and split exactly like `|J|>=2` — the jid payload keeps its affinity CPUs / `G(jid)` / its procs / `host_mem_job`; one `-` payload (same frozen timestamp) carries the unassigned CPUs, unscheduled GPUs and the node-wide rows. Before this the sole marked payload carried every CPU and node-wide row and dropped the GPUs outside the grant, with no `-` payload.
- **Title-named entries never emit `%affinity`** (no `SLURM_JOB_GPUS`; stepd fds/affinity are not the grant) and claim no CPUs/GPUs. Sole title-named entry → unmarked payload with every available GPU (an empty-grant `job_affinity` row would hide the job's GPUs). `|J|>=2` → listed in `%jobs`, no `%affinity`, payload carries only its `host_mem_job` (no CPU/GPU/proc/node-wide rows); its CPUs/GPUs stay on the `-` remainder. Decisions live in linkable `job_emit_filter.c` (`job_emit_sole_ctx`, `job_emit_multi_ctx`, `job_emit_remainder_ctx`, `job_emit_entry_cpulist`, `job_emit_entry_emits_affinity`).
- Marked tick (`|J|>=2`, or a sole partial jid): N jid payloads + one `-` node-wide payload; same frozen timestamp.
- DEBUG shm: `fast`/`full` keep last jid only; `fast.burst`/`full.burst` hold the full tick.
- GPU `dev` = collector index; unknown inventory never takes the no-mark fast path.
- Marked-tick GPU filter: each jid keeps `G(jid)`; `-` keeps **unscheduled** `G_available − ∪G(jid)` (omit GPU rows on `-` when inventory unknown).
- Marked-tick CPU filter: each jid keeps `host_cpu` / `host_cpu_hw` devices in its affinity cpulist; `-` keeps the online remainder (same split shape as GPU).

## `host_mem_job` (job cgroup memory)

- Read **only** `…/slurmstepd.scope/<token>/memory.{current,peak,stat}` (not task leaf, not bare `slurmstepd.scope`).
- `dev=j:<jid>` (literal `j:` prefix). Override root via `HPCPERFSTATS_CGROUP_ROOT` (tests).
- KEYS overlap a **subset** of `host_mem` names (`mem_used`, `anon_pages`, …) plus `mem_peak`; **not** full NUMA `host_mem` parity (`mem_total` / `active` / `slab` / … absent).
- Units `U=KB` (bytes/1024). Missing peak/stat fields → `0`. Fail-open: omit device if `memory.current` missing.
- Filter: jid payloads keep matching `j:<jid>` only; `-` payload never includes `host_mem_job`.
- Node-wide `host_mem` (NUMA) unchanged; never N-fold onto jid payloads when `|J|>=2`.
